-- section: 7.5-stdlib
-- @req: STDLIB-03, OQ-01
-- @expected-pass-after: phase-38
-- XFAIL (phase-38): Map.new() is a stub returning Void (E0202: expected
-- 'Map', got 'Void') — same Wave-4 container-rewrite gap as Set.new in
-- 7.5-stdlib/set_basic. The Hashable-key acceptance contract (E0206 ABSENT)
-- is pinned by the dedicated ctest row v4_7.5-stdlib_map_hashable_ok and
-- already holds; the runtime contract needs the real Map constructor.
-- Map[String, Int] is well-formed: String satisfies the Hashable key bound.

func main() {
    var m: Map[String, Int] = Map.new()
    m.set("one", 1)
    m.set("two", 2)
    println("one: {m.get(\"one\")}")
}
